{"type":"message","id":"6929f8b1","parentId":"95ab25de","timestamp":"2026-05-13T09:53:03.269Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Proposing a script**\n\nI see that I need to propose a script rather than create one since the user mentioned \"primero propón.\" I don't need any tools for this, and I have to focus on the Spanish language. I should include content that can be developed later, as well as the associated risks. It's about crafting a thoughtful proposal rather than delivering a final product right away. Let's get started on that!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_079b9ccb28e0a130016a0449b169648191bce883d2a992e25f\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqBEm0RcarXntHZA28Q9jqyUzAD0oZiSxMJpcGizLfZ-xF5P1HyEQv_0HcO5lLRNgVkVv11kf5_nhc9a7ZC5C99LE_oHeF9r-vfEIJeO02AAlUBPyxtGP1gWf7XJcTQNJDEfPHZGStB2zVnH1MwfZnbrQrTKnuJgfoQdSomKHmn2JvaxS4jCjEUmn6RKN7N0vOTw7X-x9WdiP6jsDlrEt94Upka3e9K2UcKBJgw5zWRDzjmgb-kcrg92JX5lBQQC5LPKn676-S4F4pn_5hr4xQ2j9D57uZQ3JWx0nEYK8cy_ff9C-2fvIKrUZjyzTRqFWy26uT4E5dEAdrRRcEbdFkCYcNOHX13HU0NIJTAIZZDrYDXN66fT1JcrI41qm0FEPmYCc8xg8-KkIXj6V8T9VMNgY06wVbxTo5CAw8s94pf89L5byfEFyCh2-s17v-cmRvP68QCpWeuNfGCG3x5Rm6o8if4QZzpB0xQKNKnUfEljlMZ9N7E4QAe3twHGXBeHp2_CIfhu_vcwQyypBZzg4yyJsewSfyOoYFsrjn5W6x2jtwCrqSsBPrZlZE1fC7fNmkGGotrZ9PInsXJ5sFuPnzD_uEtdxp1BBvc5qyDMeq26cmFX-UkHbCZkrqASpbxtCT35cBcNPFBHOd0nM1VR6BMDnnHil5LGKzFg3wEc5N9IES-zCvtowID_nVHWbjHnn29Q4x0RoZ7y1-gNQi5MXv7ABhpLjwY2LHTN4dIuONWL8CHlCtbHtPSeqZIHy5JD4Qr8gBCWVaQDaFnH1U4Ski3swraItkuWDsH2K0MEzYu45lsPiuf49UsPgkbGLxKFcBBe7-6lw7x4TnHWdp_URYOb_KD_NrODyFTJZtBmCrlLHdMDjzIUKR_1V5nSLnTEDtD9ktVFz7bEQkE_EqPsF2u99wc4JMigKNlaNWCVugLphwBwmyDsd_rKrKvxV0T4LeBYdUDB9WpZ0CjBA6qQx6f8HmGj4nQ0y3AGF9bl9gXH2XQWxrXDB17wZr8_aZhdeuYNxsxyGh_oyfwOSm2arYd5TzwRjOTQ5E81tx1G_jHKamybaMn71bctxPypTP9FC7PlHtxqmootOEA-IhYMOBdD2bfA==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Proposing a script**\\n\\nI see that I need to propose a script rather than create one since the user mentioned \\\"primero propón.\\\" I don't need any tools for this, and I have to focus on the Spanish language. I should include content that can be developed later, as well as the associated risks. It's about crafting a thoughtful proposal rather than delivering a final product right away. Let's get started on that!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"Perfecto. No ejecuto ni creo nada todavía.\n\nPropuesta de script manual read-only:\n\n`/openclaw/workspace/main/dashboard-v2/tools/generate-tokens-daily-summary.js`\n\n## Qué haría\n\n- Leer solo:\n  - `~/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions/*.jsonl`\n- Parsear cada línea JSONL.\n- Usar solo entradas con:\n  - `timestamp` válido;\n  - `usage.totalTokens > 0`.\n- Excluir del consumo:\n  - `totalTokens = 0`;\n  - entradas sin `usage`;\n  - JSON inválido;\n  - timestamps inválidos.\n- Agrupar por día local en `Europe/Madrid`.\n- Sumar:\n  - `usage.totalTokens`;\n  - `usage.input`;\n  - `usage.output`;\n  - `usage.cacheRead`;\n  - `usage.cacheWrite`;\n  - `usage.cost.total`.\n- Conservar calidad:\n  - entradas totales;\n  - válidas;\n  - cero tokens;\n  - sin usage;\n  - JSON inválidas;\n  - timestamp inválido.\n- Escribir snapshot en:\n  - `dashboard-v2/snapshots/tokens-daily-summary.json`\n\n## Script propuesto\n\n```js\n#!/usr/bin/env node\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport readline from \"node:readline\";\n\nconst TIMEZONE = \"Europe/Madrid\";\nconst SOURCE_DIR = path.join(os.homedir(), \".openclaw\", \"agents\", \"main\", \"sessions\");\nconst OUTPUT_FILE = \"/openclaw/workspace/main/dashboard-v2/snapshots/tokens-daily-summary.json\";\n\nfunction isNumber(value) {\n  return typeof value === \"number\" && Number.isFinite(value);\n}\n\nfunction addNullableNumber(target, key, value, presenceKey) {\n  if (isNumber(value)) {\n    target[key] += value;\n    target[presenceKey] += 1;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction localDay(timestamp) {\n  const date = new Date(timestamp);\n  if (Number.isNaN(date.getTime())) return null;\n\n  const parts = new Intl.DateTimeFormat(\"en-CA\", {\n    timeZone: TIMEZONE,\n    year: \"numeric\",\n    month: \"2-digit\",\n    day: \"2-digit\"\n  }).formatToParts(date);\n\n  const y = parts.find(p => p.type === \"year\")?.value;\n  const m = parts.find(p => p.type === \"month\")?.value;\n  const d = parts.find(p => p.type === \"day\")?.value;\n\n  return y && m && d ? `${y}-${m}-${d}` : null;\n}\n\nfunction emptyDay(date) {\n  return {\n    date,\n    agent: \"main\",\n    status: \"real\",\n    source: SOURCE_DIR,\n    timezone: TIMEZONE,\n    metrics: {\n      totalTokens: 0,\n      costTotal: null,\n      usageEntries: 0\n    },\n    breakdown: {\n      input: 0,\n      output: 0,\n      cacheRead: 0,\n      cacheWrite: 0\n    },\n    fieldPresence: {\n      input: 0,\n      output: 0,\n      cacheRead: 0,\n      cacheWrite: 0,\n      costTotal: 0\n    },\n    quality: {\n      entries_total: 0,\n      entries_valid_usage: 0,\n      entries_zero_total_tokens: 0,\n      entries_missing_usage: 0,\n      entries_invalid_json: 0,\n      entries_invalid_timestamp: 0\n    },\n    models_seen: [],\n    providers_seen: []\n  };\n}\n\nfunction addUnique(list, value) {\n  if (typeof value === \"string\" && value && !list.includes(value)) {\n    list.push(value);\n  }\n}\n\nasync function main() {\n  const qualityGlobal = {\n    files_read: 0,\n    entries_total: 0,\n    entries_valid_usage: 0,\n    entries_zero_total_tokens: 0,\n    entries_missing_usage: 0,\n    entries_invalid_json: 0,\n    entries_invalid_timestamp: 0\n  };\n\n  const days = new Map();\n\n  if (!fs.existsSync(SOURCE_DIR)) {\n    const snapshot = {\n      schema: \"neodaemon.tokens_daily_summary.v1\",\n      status: \"no_disponible\",\n      generated_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n      timezone: TIMEZONE,\n      source: SOURCE_DIR,\n      output: OUTPUT_FILE,\n      agent: \"main\",\n      days: [],\n      quality: qualityGlobal,\n      limitations: [\n        \"Source directory does not exist.\",\n        \"No token values were inferred.\",\n        \"Dashboard was not modified.\"\n      ]\n    };\n\n    fs.writeFileSync(OUTPUT_FILE, JSON.stringify(snapshot, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\n    return;\n  }\n\n  const files = fs.readdirSync(SOURCE_DIR)\n    .filter(name => name.endsWith(\".jsonl\"))\n    .map(name => path.join(SOURCE_DIR, name))\n    .sort();\n\n  for (const file of files) {\n    qualityGlobal.files_read += 1;\n\n    const stream = fs.createReadStream(file, { encoding: \"utf8\" });\n    const rl = readline.createInterface({ input: stream, crlfDelay: Infinity });\n\n    for await (const line of rl) {\n      if (!line.trim()) continue;\n\n      qualityGlobal.entries_total += 1;\n\n      let entry;\n      try {\n        entry = JSON.parse(line);\n      } catch {\n        qualityGlobal.entries_invalid_json += 1;\n        continue;\n      }\n\n      const day = localDay(entry.timestamp);\n      if (!day) {\n        qualityGlobal.entries_invalid_timestamp += 1;\n        continue;\n      }\n\n      if (!days.has(day)) days.set(day, emptyDay(day));\n      const dayBucket = days.get(day);\n      dayBucket.quality.entries_total += 1;\n\n      const usage = entry.usage;\n      if (!usage || typeof usage !== \"object\") {\n        qualityGlobal.entries_missing_usage += 1;\n        dayBucket.quality.entries_missing_usage += 1;\n        continue;\n      }\n\n      if (!isNumber(usage.totalTokens) || usage.totalTokens === 0) {\n        qualityGlobal.entries_zero_total_tokens += 1;\n        dayBucket.quality.entries_zero_total_tokens += 1;\n        continue;\n      }\n\n      if (usage.totalTokens < 0) {\n        qualityGlobal.entries_zero_total_tokens += 1;\n        dayBucket.quality.entries_zero_total_tokens += 1;\n        continue;\n      }\n\n      qualityGlobal.entries_valid_usage += 1;\n      dayBucket.quality.entries_valid_usage += 1;\n\n      dayBucket.metrics.totalTokens += usage.totalTokens;\n      dayBucket.metrics.usageEntries += 1;\n\n      addNullableNumber(dayBucket.breakdown, \"input\", usage.input, \"input\");\n      addNullableNumber(dayBucket.breakdown, \"output\", usage.output, \"output\");\n      addNullableNumber(dayBucket.breakdown, \"cacheRead\", usage.cacheRead, \"cacheRead\");\n      addNullableNumber(dayBucket.breakdown, \"cacheWrite\", usage.cacheWrite, \"cacheWrite\");\n\n      if (usage.cost && isNumber(usage.cost.total)) {\n        dayBucket.metrics.costTotal =\n          dayBucket.metrics.costTotal === null\n            ? usage.cost.total\n            : dayBucket.metrics.costTotal + usage.cost.total;\n        dayBucket.fieldPresence.costTotal += 1;\n      }\n\n      addUnique(dayBucket.models_seen, entry.model);\n      addUnique(dayBucket.providers_seen, entry.provider);\n    }\n  }\n\n  const snapshot = {\n    schema: \"neodaemon.tokens_daily_summary.v1\",\n    status: \"real\",\n    generated_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n    timezone: TIMEZONE,\n    source: SOURCE_DIR,\n    output: OUTPUT_FILE,\n    agent: \"main\",\n    rules: {\n      valid_usage: \"usage.totalTokens > 0 with valid timestamp\",\n      zero_total_tokens: \"excluded from consumption totals and counted in quality\",\n      grouping: \"local day in Europe/Madrid\",\n      cost: \"sum usage.cost.total only when present; null when unavailable\"\n    },\n    days: [...days.values()].sort((a, b) => a.date.localeCompare(b.date)),\n    quality: qualityGlobal,\n    limitations: [\n      \"Reads only main agent sessions.\",\n      \"Does not include task-validator sessions.\",\n      \"Usage entries are model/provider log entries, not necessarily human Telegram messages.\",\n      \"totalTokens semantics depend on OpenClaw/provider logging.\",\n      \"cacheRead/cacheWrite are preserved separately.\",\n      \"Entries with totalTokens = 0 are excluded from consumption totals.\",\n      \"Dashboard is not modified by this script.\"\n    ]\n  };\n\n  fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(OUTPUT_FILE), { recursive: true });\n  fs.writeFileSync(OUTPUT_FILE, JSON.stringify(snapshot, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\n}\n\nmain().catch(error => {\n  console.error(error);\n  process.exit(1);\n});\n```\n\n## Riesgos\n\n1. **“usageEntries” no son mensajes humanos**\n   - Son entradas de uso en sesiones JSONL.\n   - Mejor no llamarlas “mensajes” en UI final.\n\n2. **`totalTokens` puede tener semántica de proveedor**\n   - Puede incluir o no ciertos componentes.\n   - Por eso cache se conserva separado.\n\n3. **Coste no siempre fiable/comparable**\n   - `usage.cost.total` se suma solo si existe.\n   - No se calcula coste propio.\n\n4. **Solo cubre `main`**\n   - No incluye `task-validator`.\n   - Si se añade luego, debe ir separado.\n\n5. **`totalTokens = 0`**\n   - Se excluye del consumo.\n   - Se conserva en `quality`.\n\n6. **Privacidad/localidad**\n   - Lee logs locales de sesiones.\n   - No envía nada fuera.\n   - Pero el snapshot resultante puede revelar volumen de uso/coste, así que debe quedarse local.\n\n## Recomendación\n\nMe parece seguro como siguiente paso si lo dejamos en:\n\n- script manual;\n- read-only sobre sesiones;\n- snapshot local;\n- sin dashboard;\n- sin cron;\n- sin automatización.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_079b9ccb28e0a130016a0449b46e6c8191a5e753d8c27c7ac3\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":2149,"output":2161,"cacheRead":62976,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":67286,"cost":{"input":0.010745000000000001,"output":0.06483,"cacheRead":0.031487999999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.10706299999999999}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1778665902042,"responseId":"resp_079b9ccb28e0a130016a0449aebbc88191bf7f0d5095c70cc2"}}
{"type":"message","id":"751264d0","parentId":"6929f8b1","timestamp":"2026-05-13T09:54:37.214Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"El script me parece aprobado conceptualmente, pero antes de crearlo corrige este bug:\nEn localDay(), esta línea está mal:\nreturn y && m && d ? ${y}-${m}-${d} : null;\nDebe ser:\nreturn y && m && d ? ${y}-${m}-${d} : null;\nAutorizo crear el script corregido en:\ndashboard-v2/tools/generate-tokens-daily-summary.js\nRestricciones:\nno ejecutarlo todavía;\nno modificar dashboard;\nno crear cron;\nno automatizar;\nno tocar configuración.\nDespués de crearlo, resume qué archivo has creado y espera confirmación antes de ejecutarlo."}],"timestamp":1778666077213}}
