y. Should I include an optional example line? Because the user is allowed to see one, I think that would help. It could be beneficial for them to understand how it looks in practice. So, I'll definitely consider including that example line in my response to make things clearer and easier to follow!\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_hrozrXDcv66gzwDAERSzMK4z|fc_079b9ccb28e0a130016a04dd2100f88191890873591b8e7f9c","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/openclaw/workspace/main/dashboard-v2/tasks/tasks.jsonl","content":"{\"task_id\":\"example-001\",\"title\":\"ejemplo\",\"started_at\":null,\"ended_at\":null,\"status\":\"planned\",\"result\":null,\"related_files\":[],\"notes\":\"Ejemplo placeholder. No representa una task real.\"}\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":493,"output":115,"cacheRead":101888,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":102496,"cost":{"input":0.002465,"output":0.00345,"cacheRead":0.050943999999999996,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.05685899999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778703646321,"responseId":"resp_079b9ccb28e0a130016a04dd1e7c80819192f9273fc7342172"}}
